  "term": "existential phenomenology",
  "definition": "Existential phenomenology is an approach for understanding experience that focuses on the lived body and how bodily, emotional, and psychological life are deeply interconnected. In this view, meaning is grounded in how a person experiences the world through embodied existence.",
