      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that the approach focuses on the lived body and that bodily, emotional, and psychological life are “deeply interconnected,” but the packet only explicitly states that Merleau-Ponty’s existential phenomenology “emphasizes the lived body” and provides a framework for the “interplay between physical and psychological experiences.”",
        "The definition states that “meaning is grounded in how a person experiences the world through embodied existence,” which is not supported by the packet text.",
